'''Section IV''' ({{Langx|bl|Sección IV}}) is a fringe, [[List of platforms in Balisca|unrecognized platform]] established in 1963 in Balisca, originally as a "[[W:Trotskyism|Trotskyist]]–[[W:Posadist|Posadist]]" organization. It is the sole active "Trotskyist" organizations in [[Abyala]]. It has never achieved electoral representation at any level in Balisca.

In the post-Great Adonian War period, Section IV argued that [[W:Peaceful coexistence|peaceful coexistence]] had been repeatedly proven impossible due to capitalist aggression, and endorsed calls for [[W:World revolution|world revolution]], to be aided by preemptive nuclear strikes by socialist states aimed at destroying the nuclear capabilities of capitalist powers (such as [[Balisca and weapons of mass destruction|during]] the [[Camboriú War]]). Its members fervently opposed the [[Kuluba Accords]], the dismantling of Balisca's nuclear weaponry and eventual signing of the [[Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons]]. The platform has never gained mainstream appeal, often attributed to its advocacy for [[W:Nuclear war|nuclear war]], association with the extreme [[W:Rationalist community|rationalist community]] and the online activities of its proponents, considered cult-like.

Against the background of [[W:Climate collapse|climate collapse]], incipient [[W:Fascism|fascism]], and the real possibility of nuclear warfare, Section IV has received increased interest in the 21st century as a front of left-wing militancy with esoteric ideas (so called "apocalypse communism" a revolutionary imagination characterized, in part, by "an unflinching counterpoint to the [[W:Neo-fascist|neo-fascist]] politics of exclusion") in the face of [[W:Societal collapse|societal collapse]].

